{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-48385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={cos}^{4}⁡(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-48385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{4}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3}\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{u}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-48385" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa13213f4cdcefe75b7ce1892a5662eb115fdd3cca95dc4c7a249d183aa69050"} {"question" "q-48385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-48385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "-4{sin}^{3}⁡x"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,{sin}^{3}⁡x"] ["math" "4{cos}^{3}⁡x"] ["math" "4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-48385" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4{cos}^{3}⁡x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)=4{cos}^{7}⁡(x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express\n\n$$\nf(x)=4(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we see that $f(x)$ can be expressed as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=4{u}^{7},\\,u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=28{u}^{6},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =28{u}^{6}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =28(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)^{6}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x) \\\\  & =-28{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72157" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa13213f4cdcefe75b7ce1892a5662eb115fdd3cca95dc4c7a249d183aa69050"} {"question" "q-72157" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72157" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-28\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{6}⁡x"] ["math" "-28{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] ["math" "-28{sin}^{6}⁡x"] ["math" "4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{6}⁡x"] ["math" "4{cos}^{6}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72157" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-28{cos}^{6}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the derivative of $y=\\operatorname{cot}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{cot}⁡u,\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-{csc}^{2}⁡u,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =-{csc}^{2}⁡u\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72161" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa13213f4cdcefe75b7ce1892a5662eb115fdd3cca95dc4c7a249d183aa69050"} {"question" "q-72161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"] ["math" "-{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)"] ["math" "{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-72161" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{csc}^{2}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x)-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4},$ we have\n\n${f}^{′}(x)=$\n\n{{field-1}}." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Let $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x)$ and $h(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}.$ Then\n\n$$\nf(x)=g(x)+h(x).\n$$\n\nFirst, we differentiate $g(x).$ We express $g(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x)$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ng=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u,\\,u=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\,\\text{and}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sec}⁡u\\operatorname{tan}⁡u\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we differentiate $h(x)=-\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}.$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}h}{\\text{d}x} & =-{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={g}^{′}(x)+{h}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sec}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2x)-{x}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa13213f4cdcefe75b7ce1892a5662eb115fdd3cca95dc4c7a249d183aa69050"} {"question" "q-342402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sec(2x)\\tan(2x)-x^3"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that $y=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)),$ we have\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\operatorname{sec}⁡($\n{{field-2}} $)\\operatorname{tan}⁡($\n{{field-3}} $).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we express $y$ as the composite function\n\n$$\ny=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u),\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x).\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nWe now apply the chain rule, and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sec}⁡(u)\\operatorname{tan}⁡(u)\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡x \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sec}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x))\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "aa13213f4cdcefe75b7ce1892a5662eb115fdd3cca95dc4c7a249d183aa69050"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\cos(x)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007844/state.json" "file_sha256" "7b412c6f5455a26a5051401d740067ca74a9cd0b4fa0640567f8c324f1bd095e"} {"question" "q-342443" "field" "fie